SUMMARY:Creating a High School Roadmap - Parent & Teen Program
DESCRIPTION:Families with students in grades 8 through 12 often arrive at 
 junior year with very little sense of how the pieces fit together — 
 coursework\, extracurriculars\, testing timelines\, and applications. Until 
 now.\n\nIn the workshop\, attendees will walk away with:\n\n       A clear 
 picture of what each grade\, 8 through 12\,  should look like academically 
 and outside the classroom\n\n       An understanding of standardized 
 testing timelines and how to approach them without last-minute stress\n\n   
     A grounded overview of the college application and financial aid 
 process\, broken down by year\n\n       Practical language for opening 
 productive conversations between parents and students about goals\, course 
 selection\, and next steps\n\nParent & Teen Program | Registration 
 Required\nOPEN to all\n\nAbout the Presenter: Kevin Wallace is a licensed 
 master social worker and co-founder of Full Circle College and Career 
 Prep\, based in Teaneck\, NJ. Alongside his co-presenter\, Cheryl 
 Varghese\, who holds a Master of Science in School Counseling\, they work 
 directly with high school students and families across northern New Jersey.
LOCATION:Glen Ridge - Meeting Room\, Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Special Event
UID:LibCal-10286-17078474
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17078474
END:VEVENT
