SUMMARY:Courage\, Choice\, and What Comes Next with Dystopian Icon Veronica Roth
DESCRIPTION:A single choice can transform your destiny. Join us for an 
 online conversation with #1 New York Times bestselling author Veronica Roth 
 as we celebrate the enduring legacy of her Divergent series\, one of the 
 most iconic young adult series of a generation\, and get an exclusive sneak 
 peek into her highly anticipated upcoming novel\, The Sixth 
 Faction!\n\nFifteen years after readers first stepped into dystopian 
 Chicago alongside Tris Prior\, the Divergent universe continues to 
 captivate readers with its unflinching exploration of identity\, courage\, 
 and sacrifice. And in the alternate universe of The Sixth Faction\, we 
 revisit familiar characters in a completely new way… \n\nBeatrice Prior 
 stands on the brink of a decision every person in her world must make: five 
 factions\, five futures\, five lives.\n\nShe has a plan: she’s going to 
 make the bravest choice and leave Abnegation to join Dauntless\, even 
 though it means abandoning her family.\n\nBut when tragedy strikes at her 
 choosing ceremony\, everything changes—her world\, her plans\, even 
 Beatrice herself.\n\nHer decision will thrust her into the crosshairs of an 
 underground rebellion\, where a boy with secrets as dangerous as her 
 own—a boy with only a number for a name—may be the only person she can 
 trust.\n\nOne choice will change everything.\n\nRegister now for the chance 
 to ask questions and get an exclusive sneak peek of The Sixth Faction–out 
 on October 6\, 2026!\n\n \n\nAbout the Author: \n\nVeronica Roth is the #1 
 New York Times best-selling author of numerous titles including When Among 
 Crows\, Chosen Ones\, the Divergent series\, Carve the Mark and the 
 upcoming Seek the Traitor’s Son. Veronica lives with her husband and 
 their dog in Chicago\, a city that she lovingly features (and frequently 
 destroys) in many of her novels.
LOCATION:Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Author Event/Talk
