SUMMARY:Pasta with a Twist: A Fresh Take on Italian Classics with Food Network Star Joe Sasto
DESCRIPTION:It’s time to ditch the same boring recipes and bring big\, 
 playful creativity back into your kitchen! Join us for an online 
 conversation with Top Chef finalist and Food Network star Joe Sasto as we 
 explore his hit national bestselling cookbook\, Breaking the Rules: A Fresh 
 Take on Italian Classics. \n\nWhether you are a novice cook looking to 
 build your kitchen confidence or an experienced chef eager to expand your 
 culinary repertoire\, Joe’s approachable philosophy will change how you 
 view everyday ingredients. We will dive deep into his vibrant world of 
 handcrafted pasta\, step-by-step rolling techniques\, and unexpected flavor 
 profiles. \n\nFrom foundational family favorites like his mom’s red sauce 
 to daring\, crave-worthy creations like Corn Cacio e Pepe\, Marinated 
 Tomato “Amatriciana\,” and Pesto Pinwheel Pull-Apart Bread\, this 
 conversation is an open invitation to trust your culinary instincts and 
 cook with absolute freedom.\n\nRegister today and learn how to make cooking 
 fun again!\n\n \n\nAbout the Author: \n\nCelebrity chef Joe Sasto found his 
 love for cooking and appetite for Italian classics as a child at his 
 mother's side. When the COVID-19 pandemic hit in March 2020\, he pivoted 
 his career by teaching virtual pasta-making classes.\n\nWith more than half 
 a billion likes and countless viral social media videos\, Sasto has become 
 a recurring judge and chef personality across multiple shows on the Food 
 Network. He's also competed and appeared on Food Network shows such as Guy 
 Fieri's Tournament of Champions\, Guy's Grocery Games\, and Chopped\, as 
 well as Bravo's Top Chef and Top Chef All-stars.\n\nIn 2022\, Sasto made 
 the Food Network's first-ever "Hot List." Aside from his career as a chef\, 
 Sasto has developed a high-end customizable pasta and pizza tool line\, and 
 he is the creator of Tantos\, the first puffed pasta chip\, and a gourmet 
 frozen ravioli brand\, Ripi. His first cookbook\, Breaking the Rules – a 
 fresh take on Italian classics\, was published in October 2025. He lives in 
 Chicago and enjoys spending time with his pup\, Tito\, and his wife\, Kait.
LOCATION:Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Author Event/Talk
UID:LibCal-10286-17377646
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17377646
END:VEVENT
