BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261022T230000Z
DTEND:20261023T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261022T000000Z
SUMMARY:Ghosts\, Grief\, and Growing Up: YA Storytelling with Cherie Dimaline
DESCRIPTION:Step into the atmospheric and deeply moving world of 
 storytelling with acclaimed Métis author Cherie Dimaline as we discuss her 
 captivating body of work and her haunting Young Adult novel\, Funeral Songs 
 for Dying Girls.\n\nSet in a cemetery shed where sixteen-year-old Winifred 
 lives with her dad\, Funeral Songs for Dying Girls follows a teen whose 
 attempt to save her father's job leads to a fake ghost rumor—and 
 accidentally summons a very real\, opinionated spirit named Phil. Through 
 this eerie yet heartwarming story\, Dimaline crafts a haunting masterpiece 
 about grief\, survival\, identity\, and unexpected connections across the 
 boundary of life and death. \n\nBeyond her graveyard-set YA novel\, we will 
 explore Dimaline’s expansive literary career—from the groundbreaking 
 dystopian survival narrative of The Marrow Thieves and its sequel Hunting 
 by Stars\, to the dark\, magic-infused folklore of her adult novels like 
 Empire of Wild and VenCo.\n\nRegister today to participate in this 
 spellbinding conversation!\n\n \n\nAbout the Author: \n\nCherie Dimaline is 
 an internationally bestselling author. Her book The Marrow Thieves was 
 named by TIME magazine\, one of the Best YA Books of All Time and won the 
 Governor General’s Award and the Kirkus Prize. Her novel Empire of Wild 
 was an instant Canadian bestseller and is being adapted into a full opera 
 for the Canadian Opera Company. Hunting By Stars was a 2022 American Indian 
 Library Association Honor Book and her novel VENCO debuted at #1 on 
 Canadian bestseller lists. Other titles include Funeral Songs for Dying 
 Girls (AILA Honor Book\, AURA Award winner\, CRIME WRITERS Best Book\, Bram 
 Stoker Finalist) and Into the Bright Open (2024 Governor General’s Award 
 Finalist).\n\nCherie lives in her Georgian Bay Métis Community and has 
 written and produced for MARVEL\, FX\, HBO\, Disney\, and is currently 
 adapting two major projects for AMC.
LOCATION:Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Author Event/Talk
UID:LibCal-10286-17377666
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17377666
END:VEVENT
