BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261106T000000Z
DTEND:20261106T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261105T000000Z
SUMMARY:Secrets\, Lies\, and Unforgettable Twists: A Conversation with E. Lockhart
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an exciting author talk with #1 New York Times 
 bestselling author E. Lockhart as we reflect on her impressive body of 
 work\, including the literary sensation We Were Liars\, and even gain an 
 exclusive sneak peek into her shimmering new thriller\, The Pools. 
 \n\nOnce\, in a small New England town known for its hot springs\, 
 something terrible happened. Something that should have been a warning to 
 stay away from the pools\, if the stories were to be believed.\n\nBut no 
 one is afraid of the water anymore\, even if they should be.\n\nWhen new 
 girl Lexie meets golden boy Chester\, their chemistry is undeniable. 
 She’s running from a glittering life she won’t speak about. He’s 
 hiding secrets of his own. Their connection feels bigger than both of 
 them\, despite their damage.\n\nOne frigid winter morning in that small New 
 England town\, five people go for a swim in the pools. Five people\, 
 including Chester. What happens there sends shock waves through the town\, 
 changing life as Lexie knows it forever.\n\nRegister now to step into the 
 gripping\, suspenseful worlds of E. Lockhart and ask questions live!\n\n 
 \n\nAbout the Author: \n\nLockhart is the #1 New York Times bestselling 
 author of the LIARS novels: We Were Liars\, Family of Liars\, and We Fell 
 Apart. We Were Liars is also an original series on Prime Video. Her other 
 books include Again Again\, Genuine Fraud\, and The Disreputable History of 
 Frankie Landau-Banks. She has been a finalist for the Los Angeles Times 
 Book Prize and the National Book Award and an honoree for the Printz Award. 
 She lives in Brooklyn\, New York.
LOCATION:Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Author Event/Talk
UID:LibCal-10286-17567130
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17567130
END:VEVENT
