BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261111T190000Z
DTEND:20261111T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261111T000000Z
SUMMARY:How Money Became God: Rethinking Wealth and Greed in Modern Society with Paul Vigna
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an eye-opening conversation with veteran journalist 
 Paul Vigna as we examine his provocative book\, The Almightier: How Money 
 Became God\, Greed Became Virtue\, and Debt Became Sin\, in which he 
 explores the question: how did money go from a tool of commerce into the 
 dominant faith of modern society? \n\nIn The Almightier\, Vigna takes 
 readers on a sweeping historical journey from Renaissance Florence to 
 today’s global financial markets\, revealing how wealth accumulation 
 evolved from a moral failing into an unspoken civic virtue. He uncovers the 
 forgotten history of money\, tracing the uneasy and often accidental 
 alliance between wealth and religion as it developed from ancient 
 city-states to today’s secular world\, where religious devotion has 
 receded and greed has stepped in to fill the void. \n\nThrough engaging 
 anecdotes\, original research\, and fresh perspectives on the causes of the 
 many challenges we face today\, Vigna makes a compelling argument that 
 money has no power apart from the power we give it.\n\nWhether you are 
 interested in economic history\, personal finance\, or the hidden cultural 
 forces shaping modern life\, this talk is sure to pique your interest. 
 \n\nRegister today to learn more about how devotion to money has replaced 
 religion as the foundation of our society.\n\n \n\nAbout the Author: 
 \n\nPaul Vigna is an author\, journalist\, editor and speaker\, with a 
 particular focus on capital markets and cryptocurrencies. He is the author 
 of Guts: The Anatomy of The Walking Dead and coauthor of The Age of 
 Cryptocurrency and The Truth Machine. For 25 years\, he was a reporter and 
 editor for Dow Jones Newswires and the Wall Street Journal\, pioneering 
 coverage of the cryptocurrency sector. He has appeared on CNN\, CNBC\, 
 MSNBC\, Fox\, and PBS.
LOCATION:Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Author Event/Talk
UID:LibCal-10286-17573540
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17573540
END:VEVENT
