BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261120T000000Z
DTEND:20261120T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20261119T000000Z
SUMMARY:Epic Worlds and Celestial Prophecies: Exploring the Between Earth and Sky Trilogy with Rebecca Roanhorse
DESCRIPTION:Step into a sprawling world of celestial magic\, political 
 intrigue\, and ancient prophecies with New York Times bestselling author 
 Rebecca Roanhorse as we dive deep into her acclaimed Between Earth and Sky 
 trilogy. Black Sun\, Fevered Star\, and Mirrored Heavens are inspired by 
 the rich and diverse cultures of the pre-Columbian Americas\, reshaping 
 modern speculative fiction with unmissable worldbuilding.\n\nBlack Sun\, 
 the first book in the trilogy\, introduces us to the holy city of Tova. The 
 winter solstice is usually a time for celebration and renewal\, but this 
 year it coincides with a solar eclipse\, a rare celestial event proscribed 
 by the Sun Priest as an unbalancing of the world.\n\nMeanwhile\, a ship 
 launches from a distant city bound for Tova and set to arrive on the 
 solstice. The captain of the ship\, Xiala\, is a disgraced Teek whose song 
 can calm the waters around her as easily as it can warp a man’s mind. Her 
 ship carries one passenger. Described as harmless\, the passenger\, 
 Serapio\, is a young man\, blind\, scarred\, and cloaked in destiny. As 
 Xiala well knows\, when a man is described as harmless\, he usually ends up 
 being a villain.\n\nWhether you are a longtime fan of the trilogy or 
 searching for your next immersive fantasy read\, this is an event you 
 won’t want to miss out on.\n\nRegister today to go behind the scenes with 
 one of speculative fiction's most exciting voices!\n\n \n\nAbout the 
 Author: \n\nRebecca Roanhorse is a New York Times bestselling and Nebula\, 
 Hugo\, and Locus Award-winning speculative fiction writer. She has 
 published multiple award-winning short stories and novels\, including two 
 novels in The Sixth World series\, Star Wars: Resistance Reborn\, Race to 
 the Sun for the Rick Riordan imprint\, and the Hugo Award-winning epic 
 fantasy trilogy Between Earth and Sky. She was the guest editor of 
 America’s Best Science Fiction and Fantasy (2023) and a contributor to 
 the New York Times “100 Best Books of the 21st Century.” She has also 
 written for Marvel comics and games\, and her TV writing includes FX’s A 
 Murder at the End of the World\, and the Marvel series Echo for Disney . 
 She has had her own work optioned by Paramount\, Amazon Studios\, Netflix\, 
 and AMC Studios.
LOCATION:Glen Ridge Free Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Glen Ridge Library":MAILTO:events@glenridgelibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Author Event/Talk
UID:LibCal-10286-17574506
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/17574506
END:VEVENT
